#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:8
msgid "iscsi-initiator interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `iscsi-initiator` interface allows snaps to act as iSCSI initiators, "
"enabling them to discover, connect to, and manage iSCSI targets for block "
"storage access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"The interface loads kernel modules required for iSCSI operations including "
"iscsi_tcp for transport and target_core_mod for LIO functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Interface management <how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-connect-"
"interfaces>` and {ref}`Supported interfaces <ref-index_interfaces>` for "
"further details on how interfaces are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:16
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:18
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no </br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:18
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:27
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:29
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/iscsi-initiator-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"This interface controls a resource shared by the whole system. Snaps that "
"use it can be installed as parallel instances, but every instance acts on "
"the same system resource and snapd does not coordinate between them. Make "
"sure each instance manages different resources, or run only one instance at "
"a time. See {ref}`Snaps that are unsupported as parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-shared-resources>` for details.."
msgstr ""

